# minimum required Qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0
%requires(reexport) DebugUtil
%requires DebugCmdLine
%requires Util
%requires json

%modern
%no-debugging
%allow-weak-references

module VscDebugAdapter {
    version = "0.3";
    desc = "Implements Visual Studio Code Debug Adapter protocol";
    author = "Tomas Mandys <tomas.mandys@qoretechnologies.com>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
}

/** @mainpage VscDebugAdapter Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section vscdebugadapterintro Introduction to the VscDebugAdapter Module

    The %VscDebugAdapter module provides common functionality for implementing
    Visual Studio Adapter https://microsoft.github.io/debug-adapter-protocol/.

    Only subset of features is supported in Visual Studio Code IDE and in this module.

    Supported:
    - launch, and attach to a program of a remote debug server
    - source, function and exception breakpoints, with conditions, hit conditions and log messages (logpoints);
      exceptions stop the program by their type (user or system exceptions) or when no try statement of the
      debugged code catches them (uncaught exceptions; the try statements of code that cannot be debugged are not
      seen)
    - breakpoints on any statement of a line with more than one statement (column breakpoints); columns are converted
      between the UTF-16 code units of the protocol and the bytes of %Qore with the text of the line, if the file can
      be read by the adapter, otherwise a character is assumed to be a byte
    - step over, into and out, also into a chosen call of the statement (step-in targets), continue and pause of a
      thread; all threads of the program stop when one of them
      stops, and continue together, unless the \c stopAllThreads argument of the \c launch or \c attach request is
      \c false
    - threads with their names; the default names that %Qore gives threads are not shown
    - call stacks, and the local and global variables of their frames as trees: the elements of lists, the keys of
      hashes and the members of objects, also private ones, are read when they are shown, and the elements of long
      lists are paged; variables, elements, keys and members can be set to the values of expressions
    - expressions for watches, hovers and the debug console, evaluated with the variables of a frame; in the debug
      console, a line whose first word is a debugger command is processed as the command
    - loaded sources and modules, and the output of the program

    Expressions are evaluated in a separate Program with @ref Qore::PO_LOCKDOWN "PO_LOCKDOWN", which cannot access
    the file system, the network or processes; the local variables of the frame and the global variables of the
    program are copied into variables of the expression, so an assignment in an expression does not change a variable
    of the program, while the members of objects are changed in the objects.  Expressions can refer to all code of
    the program: its functions, classes, constants and other declarations, also those that are not public; the
    functions and methods that they call run in the program, with its permissions.

    Limitations:
    - data breakpoints, stepping back, jumping to a line, and restarting a frame are not supported
    - the calls that can be stepped into are the calls of user code that are known when the code is parsed; a call
      of a method of an object of an unknown class or of a call reference is not offered, and stepping into a method
      that a subclass overrides steps over the statement
    - a breakpoint is on a statement, so an expression with more than one call, such as <tt>f(g(x))</tt>, has one
      breakpoint location
    - when a thread stops, the other threads stop at their next statement, so a thread that waits, as for input,
      stops when it runs again; with \c stopAllThreads \c false, a breakpoint or a pause stops only the thread that
      reaches it
    - the client is not notified when another debugger client changes a breakpoint

    @subsection vda_v0_3
    - the conditions, hit conditions and log messages of breakpoints are checked by the debugger in the thread that hits
      a breakpoint, so that a thread does not stop and wait for the adapter at each hit, and they are shared with the
      other clients of a debug server, such as \c qdbg; a breakpoint with an invalid hit condition is not set, and
      the error is shown for the breakpoint
    - step-in targets: the \c stepInTargets request gives the calls of the current statement, and \c stepIn with a
      \c targetId steps into the chosen call
    - breakpoints can be set on any statement of a line with more than one statement: the
      \c breakpointLocations request gives the statements of a line, and a source breakpoint with a column is set on
      the statement at the column; stack frames give the columns of their statements, and their end lines are given
      as \c endLine, as the protocol defines it
    - the output of programs that are debugged in the adapter process is sent to the IDE as \c output events instead
      of being written to the channel of the protocol; see
      @ref VscDebugAdapter::VscDebugAdapter::captureProgramOutput() "VscDebugAdapter::captureProgramOutput()"
    - the adapter waits for requests and events instead of checking for them continuously, which used all the time
      of a CPU, and it ends when the IDE closes its input
    - watches and hovers load the variables of the frame when they have not been listed
    - requests without arguments, such as \c configurationDone, are also accepted with empty arguments
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5560">issue 5560</a>)
    - the \c stopOnEntry argument of a \c launch request is supported: a launched program stops at its first
      statement only when it is \c true; otherwise it runs until a breakpoint or an exception, as in other debuggers
      of Visual Studio Code; it always stopped there before; in either case the launched program runs only after the \c
      configurationDone request, so breakpoints set during the configuration phase are always honored
    - \c stopped events give the reasons of the Debug Adapter Protocol: \c "breakpoint" and
      \c "function breakpoint" with the IDs of the breakpoints that are hit in \c hitBreakpointIds, \c "entry",
      \c "pause", \c "step", and \c "exception" with the name of the exception in \c text; the reason was the
      name of the debugger event, such as \c "step" for a breakpoint, and \c text was the whole event
    - each stack frame is named after the function that its line is in, and the frame of the top-level code of the
      program is named \c "\<top level\>"; the top frame was named after the debugger event, and each other frame
      after the function called at its line
    - threads started by a launched program run until they reach a breakpoint; they stopped when they started,
      and a thread that ended was reported as stopped
    - a function breakpoint given by the name of the function only, as Visual Studio Code gives it, is set on the
      function's only variant; such breakpoints could not be set; a breakpoint that cannot be set gives the reason
      in its \c message
    - an error handling an event of the debugger is shown in the debug console of the IDE; the thread of the event
      stayed stopped without any message
    - at the end of a program that is debugged in the adapter process, the \c terminated event is sent after all
      output of the program; the output could be sent after it
    - the log file given with \c -l is written; nothing was written to it
    - lists, hashes and objects are shown as trees whose elements, keys and members, also private ones, are read when
      they are shown; the elements of long lists are paged, and elements, keys and members can be set
    - expressions are evaluated for watches, hovers and the debug console with the variables of a frame, and
      variables are set to the values of expressions
    - conditional breakpoints, hit conditions and logpoints
    - an IDE attaching to a remote debug server that cannot be reached is told why, and a session ends with a
      message when the connection to the debug server is closed
    - the \c "uncaught" exception filter: exceptions that no try statement of the debugged code catches
    - threads are shown with their current names, when the debug server gives them (see
      @ref Qore::get_thread_name(softint) "get_thread_name(tid)"), otherwise with the names in their last events
    - when a thread stops, the other threads of the program stop at their next statement and are reported as
      paused without taking the focus, and a \c continue request continues all stopped threads, as in other
      debuggers of Visual Studio Code; the \c stopAllThreads argument of \c launch and \c attach requests set to
      \c false stops only the thread that reaches a breakpoint or is paused
    - attaching to a program of a remote debug server: the IDE can set its breakpoints as soon as the program is
      attached; threads that were stopped when it was attached, threads that the runtime stops at their next
      statement when it is attached, and threads that start during the configuration phase run on after the
      \c configurationDone request; they were not resumed and not reported as stopped

    @subsection vda_v0_2
    - updated to use a Logger

    @subsection vda_v0_1
    - initial release
*/

#! the VscDebugAdapter namespace contains all the definitions in the VscDebugAdapter module
public namespace VscDebugAdapter {
#! class that can be used for logging
public class VscDebugLogger inherits Logger {
    public {
        VscDebugAdapter debugAdapter;
    }

    private:internal {
        bool m_logging = True;
    }

    constructor(*string filename, bool appendToLog) {
        setLevel("INFO");
        if (filename.val()) {
            VscLoggerAppender appender(self, "vsc-file-appender", filename);
            addAppender(appender);

            try {
                mkdir_ex(dirname(filename), 0755, True);
                if (!appendToLog) {
                    # zero out file
                    File f();
                    f.open2(filename, O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY);
                }
                # the appender writes nothing until it is opened
                appender.open();
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                stderr.printf("%s\n", get_exception_string(ex));
                m_logging = False;
            }

        }
    }
}

class VscLoggerAppender inherits LoggerAppenderFile {
    private {
        VscDebugLogger logger;
    }

    constructor(VscDebugLogger logger, string name, string filename)
            : LoggerAppenderFile(name, new LoggerLayoutPattern("%m\r\n"), filename) {
        self.logger := logger;
    }

    #! Processes open, log, and close events with the output stream; all other events are ignored
    processEventImpl(int type, auto params) {
        LoggerAppenderFile::processEventImpl(type, params);
        if (logger.debugAdapter) {
            if (type == EVENT_LOG) {
                # the message has the line ending of the log file, which is replaced with a newline
                string line = params;
                line =~ s/\r?\n$//;
                logger.debugAdapter.printfImpl("%s\n", line);
            }
        }
    }
}

#! Visual Studio Code debug adapter class
/**
    VSC launches adapter executable and communicates over stdin and stdout. The class implements
    common functionality and provides abstract interface to connect debug server
*/
public class VscDebugAdapter inherits DebugCommandLine {
    private:internal {
        const START_LAUNCH = 1;
        const START_ATTACH = 2;
        const START_ATTACH_SUSPENDED = 3;
        const DEBUGVAR_PREFIX = "$";
        #! the name of the stack frame of the top-level code of a program
        const TopLevelFrameName = "<top level>";
        #! the first variable reference of a structured value; the references below it are those of stack frames
        const VarRefBase = 0x40000000;

        #! process loop flag
        bool m_running = True;

        #! initialize command arguments
        hash m_initializeArgs;
        #! the lines of the files read for the conversion of columns, keyed by path; values are hashes with the
        #! keys mtime, size and lines
        hash<string, hash<auto>> m_fileLines;

        #! program stat information
        hash m_programState;

        #! queue if incomming events from debug server
        Queue m_queue();

        #! queue for VSC Output window
        Queue m_outputQueue();

        #! Sequence for events passed to VSC frontend
        Sequence m_sequence(1);

        #! Sequence for loaded source reference
        Sequence m_source(1);

        #! vsc program
        int m_currentPgmId;

        #! serializes the handling of requests and events, and the messages to the IDE
        Mutex m_lock();

        #! the file that messages to the IDE are written to
        File m_out = stdout;

        #! captures the output of programs; see captureProgramOutput()
        *DebugOutputCapture m_outputCapture;

        #! events sent after the output of programs, with the number of marks of the pipes to wait for
        list<hash<auto>> m_eventsAfterOutput = ();

        #! the structured values of stopped threads, by their variable reference; see getVarRef()
        hash<string, hash<auto>> m_varRefs = {};

        #! the next variable reference of a structured value
        int m_nextVarRef = VarRefBase;

    }

    public {
        #! use program name unless not specified in launch/attach command
        *string defaultProgram;
    }

    constructor(*Logger::LoggerInterface logger) : DebugCommandLine(logger) {
        showFullException = True;
    }

    #! send command to debug server
    public *hash doCommand(hash data) {
        return DebugCommandLine::doCommand(data, False);
    }

    #! push event from debug server in queue
    public nothing pushEvent(auto event) {
        if (event.type != "vsc_output") {
            debug("Event: %y", event);
        }
        m_queue.push(event);
    }

    #! Ends the debug session when the connection to a remote debug server has been closed
    /** The client is told why in its debug console, and the session ends; may be called in any thread

        @param reason the reason that is shown to the user
    */
    public serverClosed(string reason) {
        pushEvent({"type": "vsc_server_closed", "reason": reason});
    }

    #! implement printing to console
    public printfImpl(string fmt, ...) {
        pushEvent((
            "type": "vsc_output",
            "category": "console",  # it goes to Debug Console regardless category.
            "output": vsprintf(fmt, argv)
        ));
    }

    #! run processing loop till @ref m_running is True
    /** Requests are read from stdin and handled in the calling thread, and events from the debug server and the
        output of programs are handled in a background thread; the handling of requests and events is serialized, so
        no event is handled while a request is handled.  The loop ends when a request such as \c disconnect ends
        the session or when the IDE closes the input.
    */
    public run() {
        Counter events_done(1);
        background processEvents(events_done);
        try {
            info("Run: %y", now_us());
            while (m_running) {
                *string s = readVscMessage();
                if (!exists s) {
                    # the IDE closed the input
                    break;
                }
                debug("%s", s);
                m_lock.lock();
                on_exit m_lock.unlock();
                handleVscRequest(s);
            }
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            info("ex: %y", ex);
            stopEvents(events_done);
            rethrow;
        }
        stopEvents(events_done);
        sendVscEvent("terminated");
    }

    #! Sends the output of programs that are debugged in this process to the IDE as output events
    /** The adapter communicates with the IDE on stdout, which the programs that it runs share with it.  The
        protocol is therefore written to a duplicate of stdout, and the standard output and standard error of the
        process are redirected to pipes whose contents are sent as \c "stdout" and \c "stderr" output events.

        @return @ref True if the output is captured, @ref False if it is already captured or if stdout and stderr
        cannot be duplicated on this platform; the output of programs is then written to stdout and stderr

        @par Example:
        @code{.py}
VscDebugAdapter vda = new VscDebugAdapterLocal(logger, dpc, opts);
vda.captureProgramOutput();
on_exit vda.stopProgramOutputCapture();
vda.run();
        @endcode

        @see stopProgramOutputCapture()
    */
    public bool captureProgramOutput() {
        if (m_outputCapture) {
            return False;
        }
        DebugOutputCapture capture(
            sub (string category, string output) {
                pushEvent({"type": "vsc_output", "category": category, "output": output});
            },
            # a pipe's output before a flush mark has been queued; see sendVscEventAfterOutput()
            sub (string category) {
                pushEvent({"type": "vsc_output_mark"});
            });
        try {
            if (!capture.start()) {
                return False;
            }
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            debug("the output of programs is not captured: %s", get_exception_string(ex));
            return False;
        }
        m_outputCapture = capture;
        # the protocol is written to the original stdout
        m_out = capture.getStdout();
        return True;
    }

    #! Returns the capture of the output of programs, if it is captured
    *DebugOutputCapture getOutputCapture() {
        return m_outputCapture;
    }

    #! Restores stdout and stderr after captureProgramOutput()
    /** Waits until the output that was written before has been queued for the IDE, also if a process that a program
        started still has the pipes open.
    */
    public stopProgramOutputCapture() {
        if (!m_outputCapture) {
            return;
        }
        m_outputCapture.stop();
        m_out = stdout;
        remove m_outputCapture;
    }

    #! Sends an event to the IDE after all output that programs have written
    /** The output of programs is read from pipes in other threads, so it can be queued after an event that a program
        sends when it has written it.  A flush mark is written to the pipes; each thread that forwards the output
        queues the output before the mark and then a \c "vsc_output_mark" message, and the event is sent when the
        messages of both pipes have been handled (see processEvents()).

        To be called in the thread that handles the events

        @param event the name of the event
        @param body the body of the event, if any
    */
    private:internal sendVscEventAfterOutput(string event, *hash<auto> body) {
        if (!m_outputCapture) {
            sendVscEvent(event, body);
            return;
        }
        push m_eventsAfterOutput, {"event": event, "body": body, "marks": 2};
        m_outputCapture.flush();
    }

    #! Stops the thread of processEvents() after the events that are queued
    private:internal stopEvents(Counter events_done) {
        m_queue.push({"type": "vsc_stop"});
        events_done.waitForZero();
    }

    #! Handles events from the debug server and output until the stop event
    private:internal processEvents(Counter done) {
        on_exit done.dec();
        while (True) {
            auto msg = m_queue.get();
            if (msg.type == "vsc_stop") {
                break;
            }
            m_lock.lock();
            on_exit m_lock.unlock();
            try {
                # event from debug server
                if (msg.type == "event") {
                    processDebugEvent(msg);
                } else if (msg.type == "vsc_output") {
                    sendVscEvent("output", {"category": msg.category, "output": msg.output});
                } else if (msg.type == "vsc_server_closed") {
                    # the debug server cannot be reached any more; see serverClosed()
                    sendVscEvent("output", {"category": "important", "output": msg.reason + "\n"});
                    sendVscEvent("terminated");
                } else if (msg.type == "vsc_output_mark") {
                    # a pipe's output before a flush mark has been sent; see sendVscEventAfterOutput()
                    if (m_eventsAfterOutput && !--m_eventsAfterOutput[0].marks) {
                        hash<auto> e = shift m_eventsAfterOutput;
                        sendVscEvent(e.event, e.body);
                    }
                }
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                info("ex: %y", ex);
                # the error is shown in the debug console of the IDE; otherwise a thread whose event could not be
                # handled would stay stopped without the IDE showing why
                try {
                    sendVscEvent("output", {
                        "category": "console",
                        "output": sprintf("error handling a debugger event: %s\n", get_exception_string(ex)),
                    });
                } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex1) {
                    # the IDE cannot be reached; the error is logged above
                    info("ex: %y", ex1);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    #! Reads the next message from the IDE
    /** @return the content of the message, or @ref nothing at the end of the input
    */
    private:internal *string readVscMessage() {
        int len = -1;
        binary line;
        while (True) {
            *binary c = stdin.readBinary(1);
            if (!exists c) {
                return NOTHING;
            }
            if (c == <0A>) {
                if (!line.size()) {
                    # the end of the headers
                    if (len > 0) {
                        *binary content = stdin.readBinary(len);
                        if (!exists content || content.size() < len) {
                            return NOTHING;
                        }
                        return content.toString("UTF-8");
                    }
                    # a message without content is ignored
                    len = -1;
                    continue;
                }
                *list<auto> l = line.toString("UTF-8") =~ x/^([A-Za-z\-]+):(.+)$/;
                if (l[0] == "Content-Length") {
                    len = int(trim(l[1]));
                    debug("Content-Length: %d", len);
                }
                remove line;
            } else if (c != <0D>) {
                line += c;
            }
        }
    }

    #! Handles a request from the IDE and sends the response
    private:internal handleVscRequest(string s) {
        hash request;
        hash resp.type = "response";
        try {
            request = parseVscRequest(s);
            string m = "vsc_" + request.command;
            if (!self.hasCallableMethod(m)) {
                throw "VDA-ERROR", sprintf("Command %y not implemented", request.command);
            }
            if (!m_initializeArgs && request.command != "initialize") {
                throw "VDA-ERROR", "Debug adapter is not initialized";
            }
            auto r = call_object_method(self, m, request.arguments);
            resp.success = True;
            if (r) {
                resp.body = r;
            }
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            resp.success = False;
            # the error of a command of the debugger is given without the error of the command that it was sent with
            resp.message = VscDebugAdapter::getErrorText(ex);
            debug("%s", get_exception_string(ex));
        }
        resp.request_seq = request.seq;
        resp.command = request.command;
        sendVscMessage(resp);
    }

    #! execute command (and exit)
    public execute(string cmd) {
        auto res;
        switch (cmd) {
            case 'pgmlist':
                res = doCommand(('cmd': 'program//list', 'listFiles': True));
                break;
            default:
                throw "VDA-ERROR", sprintf("Unknown command: %y", cmd);
        }
        stdout.write(make_json(res)+"\r\n");
    }

    private:internal auto resolveValue(string name, *string val, hash strings, auto defVal) {
        if (exists val) {
            if (!exists strings{val}) {
                throw "VDA-ERROR", sprintf("%y value %y is not found in %y", name, val, keys strings);
            }
            return strings{val};
        } else {
            return defVal;
        }
    }

    #! process event from debugger
    private:internal processDebugEvent(hash event) {
        if (exists event.pgmid) {
            if (!exists m_programState{event.pgmid}.info || !exists m_programState{event.pgmid}.loadedSourceById) {
                updateProgramCache(doCommand(("cmd": "program/="+event.pgmid+"/list", "listFiles": True)));
            }
        }
        debug("processDebugEvent: %y", event);
        switch (event.cmd) {
        case "interrupt":
            if (event.func == "detach") {
                detach(event);
            } else {
                if (!m_programState{event.pgmid}.vcsNotified) {
                    hash e;
                    e.name = m_programState{event.pgmid}.info.scriptName;
                    switch (m_programState{event.pgmid}.startMethod) {
                    case START_LAUNCH:
                        e.startMethod = "launch";
                        e.isLocalProcess = True;
                        break;
                    case START_ATTACH:
                        e.startMethod = "attach";
                        e.isLocalProcess = False;
                        break;
                    case START_ATTACH_SUSPENDED:
                    }
                    sendVscEvent("process", e);
                    m_programState{event.pgmid}.vcsNotified = True;
                    m_programState{event.pgmid}.mainThreadId = gettid();
                }
                # the name of the thread, which it may have changed since its last event
                m_programState{event.pgmid}.threadNames{event.tid} = event.threadname;
                if (!m_programState{event.pgmid}.vcsThreadNotified{event.tid}) {
                    sendVscEvent("thread", ("threadId": event.tid, "reason": "started"));
                    m_programState{event.pgmid}.vcsThreadNotified{event.tid} = True;
                }
                # another thread of a launched or attached program, such as one started with the background operator,
                # attaches when it starts; it runs until it reaches a breakpoint, as the program would without the
                # debugger.  A thread of an attached program that starts before the configuration phase has ended is
                # held until the client has set its breakpoints; vsc_configurationDone() resumes it.
                if (event.func == "attach" && m_programState{event.pgmid}.startMethod != START_ATTACH_SUSPENDED
                    && m_programState{event.pgmid}.startThreadId != event.tid) {
                    if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.startMethod == START_ATTACH
                        && !m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.configurationDone) {
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.heldThreads += (event.tid,);
                        return;
                    }
                    resumeThread(event.tid);
                    return;
                }
                # True if the thread stopped at the first statement of a launched program
                bool entry = False;
                if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.startMethod == START_LAUNCH && m_programState{event.pgmid}.startThreadId == event.tid) {
                    # skip debugging of bootstrap
                    if (event.func == "attach") {
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.processFlag = 1;
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.file = event.intrInfo.file;
                        # The DAP protocol requires a launched program not to run until the client has finished the
                        # configuration phase (set its breakpoints) and sent "configurationDone".  Hold the program
                        # at this first bootstrap stop until then, so that it cannot run - and a short program
                        # cannot finish and be removed - before a "setBreakpoints" request is handled against it.
                        # vsc_configurationDone() resumes it.  If "configurationDone" has already been received, do
                        # not hold: continue the bootstrap at once.  This is a race-free handshake in both
                        # directions, as the request and event handling are serialized by m_lock.
                        if (!m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.configurationDone) {
                            m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.entryHold = event;
                            return;
                        }
                    } else if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.processFlag == 1 && event.file != m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.file) {
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.processFlag = 2;
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.frameCnt = event.framecnt-1;
                        # the first statement of the program: it stops there only with "stopOnEntry", which is
                        # true when it is not given, or at a breakpoint on the statement; as the thread arrives there
                        # by a step, the event does not give the breakpoint.  The program was held at the attach stop
                        # until "configurationDone", so the client's breakpoints are already created and the decision
                        # below is final.
                        entry = True;
                    } else if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.processFlag == 2 && event.file == m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.file) {
                        # we want exit event, so we cannot detach
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.processFlag = 3;
                    }
                    switch (m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.processFlag) {
                    case 3:
                        if (event.func == "exit" || event.func == "detach") {
                            break;
                        }
                        # no break
                    case 1:
                        vsc_stepIn(("threadId": event.tid));
                        return;
                    }
                }
                # a step of the client; it ends when the thread is reported as stopped or runs without a step
                bool stepping = boolean(m_programState{event.pgmid}.steppingThreads{event.tid});
                # a thread that stops at a statement without a breakpoint, and that the client did not step or pause:
                # - when all threads stop together, a thread that another thread's stop has stopped, which is reported
                #   as paused
                # - when a client attaches to a running program, the runtime stops each thread of the program at its
                #   next statement; the thread is handled as a thread that attaches: it runs on, after the configuration
                #   phase
                # - when all threads stop together, a thread whose stop was requested before the client continued all
                #   threads, as the thread was waiting; it runs on
                if (event.func == "step" && !exists event.bkptid && !stepping
                    && !m_programState{event.pgmid}.pauseRequests{event.tid}) {
                    if (remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.allStopRequests{event.tid}) {
                        setStoppedThread(event);
                        sendVscEvent("stopped", {
                            "reason": "pause",
                            "description": "Paused as another thread stopped",
                            "threadId": event.tid,
                            "preserveFocusHint": True,
                        });
                        return;
                    }
                    if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.startMethod == START_ATTACH
                        && !m_programState{event.pgmid}.bootstrap.configurationDone) {
                        m_programState{event.pgmid}.heldThreads += (event.tid,);
                        return;
                    }
                    if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.startMethod == START_ATTACH
                        || m_programState{event.pgmid}.stopAllThreads) {
                        resumeThread(event.tid);
                        return;
                    }
                }
                # an exception stops the thread if its type is selected, or if it is not caught and uncaught exceptions
                # are selected
                if (event.func == "exception" && !VscDebugAdapter::stopsAtException(event,
                    m_programState{event.pgmid}.exceptionBreakpoints.filters)) {
                    refuseInterrupt(event);
                    break;
                }
                if (event.func == "exit" || event.func == "detach") {
                    # a thread that ends is not reported as stopped; the IDE is told that it ended
                    if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.startThreadId == event.tid) {
                        sendVscEvent("exited", ("exitCode": int(event.result)));
                    } else {
                        sendVscEvent("thread", ("threadId": event.tid, "reason": "exited"));
                    }
                    detach(event);
                    break;
                }
                # the breakpoints that stop the thread: a breakpoint with a condition or a hit condition stops it
                # only when they are met, and a logpoint writes its message and does not stop it
                list<int> hits = getHitBreakpoints(event, entry);
                list<int> ids = getStoppingBreakpoints(event, hits);
                if (!ids && (hits || entry) && !hasOtherStopReason(event, entry)) {
                    resumeThread(event.tid);
                    return;
                }
                hash<auto> e = getStopInfo(event, entry, ids);
                e.threadId = event.tid;
                setStoppedThread(event);
                sendVscEvent("stopped", e);
                if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.stopAllThreads) {
                    stopOtherThreads(event.pgmid, event.tid);
                }
            }
            break;
        case "run":
            remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.thread{event.tid};
            # a thread that runs without a step, or that has ended, is not stepped by the client
            if (event.runstate == DebugRunStateName::Run || event.runstate == DebugRunStateName::Detach) {
                remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.steppingThreads{event.tid};
            }
            # the variable references of a thread are valid while it is stopped
            removeVarRefs(event.tid);
            if (event.runstate == "attach") {
                remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.detachedThreads{event.tid};
            }
            if (event.runstate == "detach") {
                remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.vcsThreadNotified{event.tid};
                remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.pauseRequests{event.tid};
                m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.detachedThreads{event.tid} = True;
                if (!getThreads()) {
                    doCommand(("cmd": "shutdown"));
                    # the program has ended: the IDE gets all of its output before the end of the session
                    sendVscEventAfterOutput("terminated");
                }

            } else {
                sendVscEvent("continued", ("threadId": event.tid, "allThreadsContinued": False));
            }
            break;
        case "welcome":
            info("Connected: %y", event.result);
            break;
        case "output":
            # the output of the programs of a remote debug server
            sendVscEvent("output", {"category": event.category, "output": event.output});
            break;
        }
    }

    #! Returns the IDs of the source and function breakpoints of the given program on the given statement
    private:internal list<int> getBreakpointsOnStatement(softstring pgmId, *softint statementId) {
        if (!exists statementId) {
            return ();
        }
        list<int> ids = ();
        foreach hash<auto> source_bkpts in (m_programState{pgmId}.sourceBreakpoints.iterator()) {
            foreach hash<auto> i in (source_bkpts.pairIterator()) {
                if (i.value.statementId == statementId) {
                    push ids, int(i.key);
                }
            }
        }
        foreach hash<auto> i in (m_programState{pgmId}.functionBreakpoints.pairIterator()) {
            if (i.value.statementId == statementId) {
                push ids, int(i.key);
            }
        }
        return ids;
    }

    #! Returns the reason of a stop as the Debug Adapter Protocol gives it
    /** @param event the interrupt event of the stopped thread
        @param entry True if the thread stopped at the first statement of a launched program

        @return the \c reason and \c description of the \c stopped event; with \c hitBreakpointIds when the thread
        stopped at breakpoints of the client, and with \c text, the name of the exception, when it stopped at an
        exception
    */
    #! Returns the IDs of the breakpoints that the given stop of a thread is at
    /** A thread that arrives at the first statement of a launched program by a step does not report the breakpoints
        on the statement
    */
    private:internal list<int> getHitBreakpoints(hash<auto> event, bool entry) {
        # a debugger that checks the breakpoints of the statement gives all those that stop the thread
        if (event.bkptids) {
            return map int($1), event.bkptids;
        }
        return exists event.bkptid
            ? (int(event.bkptid),)
            : (entry ? getBreakpointsOnStatement(event.pgmid, event.statementid) : ());
    }

    #! Returns the IDs of the breakpoints that stop the thread among the given ones
    /** The debugger checks the conditions, hit conditions and log messages of breakpoints (see
        @ref DebugProgramControl::DebugProgramControl::checkBreakpoint() "DebugProgramControl::checkBreakpoint()"): a
        breakpoint that is the only reason of a stop has stopped the thread, and the breakpoints on the statement that
        a thread arrived at by a step at the start of a launched program are checked by the thread
    */
    private:internal list<int> getStoppingBreakpoints(hash<auto> event, list<int> hits) {
        if (exists event.bkptid || !hits) {
            return hits;
        }
        return doCommand((
            "cmd": "thread/breakpoint/check",
            "tid": event.tid,
            "value": {"ids": hits},
        )).result.stop ?? ();
    }

    #! Returns True if a thread stops for another reason than breakpoints
    /** The thread stops for a pause request, at the first statement of a launched program with \c stopOnEntry, and
        when it was stepping
    */
    private:internal bool hasOtherStopReason(hash<auto> event, bool entry) {
        if (m_programState{event.pgmid}.pauseRequests{event.tid}) {
            return True;
        }
        if (entry) {
            return m_programState{event.pgmid}.launchArgs.stopOnEntry === True;
        }
        return event.runstate != DebugRunStateName::Run;
    }

    #! Returns True if a thread stops at an exception with the given exception filters of the client
    /** @param event the exception event, with the \c exception and, from debug servers that give it, \c uncaught
        @param filters the selected filters: \c "User" and \c "System" for all exceptions of the type, and
        \c "uncaught" for exceptions that no try statement of the debugged code catches
    */
    static bool stopsAtException(hash<auto> event, *softlist<string> filters) {
        return inlist(event.exception.type, filters) || (inlist("uncaught", filters) && event.uncaught);
    }

    #! Keeps the state of a thread that is reported as stopped; a step of the client ends with the stop
    private:internal setStoppedThread(hash<auto> event) {
        remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.steppingThreads{event.tid};
        m_programState{event.pgmid}.thread{event.tid}.frameId = event.frame;
        m_programState{event.pgmid}.thread{event.tid}.debugVar = event.debugvar;
        m_programState{event.pgmid}.thread{event.tid}.exception = event.exception;
    }

    #! Returns the text of an error; the error of a command sent to a thread is given without the command's error
    static string getErrorText(hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
        return ex.err == "DEBUG-COMMAND" ? ex.desc : sprintf("%s: %s", ex.err, ex.desc);
    }

    #! Evaluates an expression with the top frame of a stopped thread
    /** @return the result of the \c thread/evaluate command: a description of the value with the \c id, \c bool
        and \c text keys
    */
    private:internal hash<auto> evaluateInThread(int tid, string expr, int frameId = 0) {
        return doCommand((
            "cmd": "thread/evaluate",
            "tid": tid,
            "frameid": frameId,
            "expression": expr,
        )).result;
    }

    private:internal hash<auto> getStopInfo(hash<auto> event, bool entry, list<int> ids) {
        # a pause request of the client is answered by the next stop of the thread
        bool pause = boolean(remove m_programState{event.pgmid}.pauseRequests{event.tid});
        switch (event.func) {
            case "exception":
                return hash<auto>{
                    "reason": "exception",
                    "description": "Paused on exception",
                    "text": event.exception.err,
                };
            case "attach":
                return hash<auto>{"reason": "entry", "description": "Paused on entry"};
        }
        if (ids) {
            # only the breakpoints of the client are reported; a breakpoint can also be created by another client
            # of the debugged program
            list<int> source_ids = select ids, isSourceBreakpoint(event.pgmid, $1);
            list<int> function_ids = select ids, exists m_programState{event.pgmid}.functionBreakpoints{$1};
            hash<auto> rv = source_ids || !function_ids
                ? hash<auto>{"reason": "breakpoint", "description": "Paused on breakpoint"}
                : hash<auto>{"reason": "function breakpoint", "description": "Paused on function breakpoint"};
            if (source_ids || function_ids) {
                rv.hitBreakpointIds = source_ids + function_ids;
            }
            return rv;
        }
        if (entry) {
            return hash<auto>{"reason": "entry", "description": "Paused on entry"};
        }
        if (pause) {
            return hash<auto>{"reason": "pause", "description": "Paused"};
        }
        return hash<auto>{"reason": "step", "description": "Paused on step"};
    }

    #! Returns True if the given breakpoint is a source breakpoint of the client in the given program
    private:internal bool isSourceBreakpoint(softstring pgmId, int id) {
        foreach hash<auto> source_bkpts in (m_programState{pgmId}.sourceBreakpoints.iterator()) {
            if (exists source_bkpts{id}) {
                return True;
            }
        }
        return False;
    }

    #! refuse interrupt and continue
    private:internal refuseInterrupt(hash event) {
        doCommand(("cmd": "thread/go", "tid": event.tid));
    }

    #! detach interrupt
    private:internal detach(hash event) {
        doCommand(("cmd": "thread/go/detach", "tid": event.tid));
    }

    #! parse request from VSC frontend
    private:internal hash parseVscRequest(string msg) {
        auto req = parse_json(msg);
        debug("receiveVsc: %y", req);
        if (req.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
            throw "VDA-ERROR", "Invalid message datatype";
        }
        if (req.type != "request") {
            throw "VDA-ERROR", sprintf("Wrong type: %y", req.type);
        }
        return req;
    }

    #! send message for VSC frontend
    private:internal sendVscMessage(hash msg) {
        if (msg.event != "output") {
            debug("sendVsc: %y", msg);
        }
        string resp = make_json(msg);
        binary b = binary(resp);
        m_out.printf("Content-Length: %d\r\n\r\n", b.size());
        m_out.write(b);
    }

    #! send event for VSC frontend
    private:internal sendVscEvent(string event, auto payload) {
        hash h;
        h.type = "event";
        h.event = event;
        h.seq = m_sequence.next();
        if (payload) {
            h.body = payload;
        }
        sendVscMessage(h);
    }

    private:internal string getLoadedSourceName(string file, *string source) {
        if (exists source) {
            return file + '@' + source;
        } else {
            return file;
        }
    }

    private:internal updateProgramCache(*hash response) {
        foreach string pgmId in (keys response.result) {
            if (!response.result{pgmId}.scriptName.val()) {
                continue;
            }
            hash e;
            if (exists m_programState{pgmId}.info) {
                e.reason = "changed";
            } else {
                e.reason = "new";
            }
            m_programState{pgmId}.info = response.result{pgmId};
            e.module = getModule(pgmId);
            sendVscEvent("module", e);
            remove e;
            if (response.result{pgmId}.debugging) {
                foreach string f in (keys response.result{pgmId}.files) {
                    string lsn = getLoadedSourceName(f);
                    *hash ls = m_programState{pgmId}.loadedSourceByName{lsn};
                    if (!exists ls) {
                        ls = (
                            'id': m_source.next(),
                            'file': f,
                        );
                        m_programState{pgmId}.loadedSourceByName{lsn} = ls;
                        m_programState{pgmId}.loadedSourceById{ls.id} = ls;
                        e.reason = "new";
                    } else {
                        e.reason = "changed";
                    }
                    e.source = getSource(ls);
                    sendVscEvent("loadedSource", e);

                    foreach string l in (keys response.result{pgmId}.files{f}) {
                        lsn = getLoadedSourceName(l, f);
                        ls = m_programState{pgmId}.loadedSourceByName{lsn};
                        if (!exists ls) {
                            ls = (
                                'id': m_source.next(),
                                'file': l,
                                'source': f,
                            );
                            m_programState{pgmId}.loadedSourceByName{lsn} = ls;
                            m_programState{pgmId}.loadedSourceById{ls.id} = ls;
                            e.reason = "new";
                        } else {
                            e.reason = "changed";
                        }
                        e.source = getSource(ls);
                        sendVscEvent("loadedSource", e);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    private:internal setThreadFrame(int threadId, int frameId) {
        if (m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.frameId !== frameId) {
            doCommand((
                "cmd": "thread/debug/frame/set",
                "tid": threadId,
                "value": frameId,
            ));
            m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.frameId = frameId;
        }
    }

    private:internal deleteBreakpoints(*hash bkpts) {
        foreach string bkptId in (keys bkpts) {
            doCommand((
                "cmd": "program//breakpoint/"+bkptId+"/delete",
            ));
        }
    }

    private:internal list setBreakpoints(*list bkptRefs) {
        list res = ();
        foreach hash bkpt in (bkptRefs) {
            hash b;
            try {
                hash bs = doCommand((
                    "cmd": "program/"+m_currentPgmId+"/breakpoint//create",
                    "value": bkpt,
                )).result;
                b.id = bs.bkptid;
                b.verified = True;
                b.statementId = bs.stmtid;  # internal
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                b.verified = False;
                # the IDE shows why the breakpoint could not be set
                b.message = ex.desc;
            }
            push res, b;
        }
        return res;
    }

    private:internal hash getModule(softint pgmId) {
        hash m;
        m.id = pgmId;
        m.name = m_programState{pgmId}.info.scriptName;
        m.file = m_programState{pgmId}.info.scriptPath;
        m.isUserCode = m_programState{pgmId}.info.debugging;
        return m;
    }

    #! Returns a source of the protocol for a loaded source
    /** A source that is a file that exists is given by its path, so that the IDE shows the file itself, where it
        shows the values of variables in hovers; other sources, such as labels and code loaded at run time, and the
        files of remote programs that do not exist here, are given by a reference, whose text is read with the
        \c source request
    */
    private:internal hash getSource(hash ls) {
        if (!ls.source.val() && ls.file =~ /^\// && is_file(ls.file)) {
            return {"name": basename(ls.file), "path": ls.file, "sourceReference": 0};
        }
        hash src;

        src.name = exists ls.source ? sprintf("Label: %s", ls.source) : sprintf("File: %s", ls.file);
        src.sourceReference = ls.id;
        src.path = ls.file;
        if (src.path =~ /^<(.*)>$/) {
            src.path =~ s/^<run-time-loaded: (.*)>$/$1/;
            # tricky as all breakpoint commands are hidden in VSC if path does not satisfy its format
            # trial/error I found it need an extension
            src.path += '.q';
        }
        return src;
    }

    #! Returns the 0-based byte column of a column of the protocol in a line
    /** @param line the text of the line, if known; without it, each character is assumed to be one byte
        @param column the column of the protocol, which counts UTF-16 code units
        @param columnsStartAt1 if the columns of the protocol start at 1

        @return the 0-based byte column of the character at the column; columns after the end of the line are
        counted from its end
    */
    static int getByteColumn(*string line, int column, bool columnsStartAt1 = True) {
        int units = column - (columnsStartAt1 ? 1 : 0);
        if (units <= 0) {
            return 0;
        }
        if (!exists line) {
            return units;
        }
        int bytes = 0;
        int len = line.length();
        for (int i = 0; i < len && units > 0; ++i) {
            string c = line[i];
            units -= c.getUnicode() > 0xffff ? 2 : 1;
            bytes += c.size();
        }
        # a column after the end of the line
        return bytes + (units > 0 ? units : 0);
    }

    #! Returns the column of the protocol of a 0-based byte column in a line
    /** @param line the text of the line, if known; without it, each character is assumed to be one byte
        @param byteColumn the 0-based byte column
        @param columnsStartAt1 if the columns of the protocol start at 1

        @return the column of the protocol, which counts UTF-16 code units
    */
    static int getProtocolColumn(*string line, int byteColumn, bool columnsStartAt1 = True) {
        int units = 0;
        if (!exists line) {
            units = byteColumn;
        } else {
            int bytes = 0;
            int len = line.length();
            for (int i = 0; i < len && bytes < byteColumn; ++i) {
                string c = line[i];
                units += c.getUnicode() > 0xffff ? 2 : 1;
                bytes += c.size();
            }
            # a column after the end of the line
            if (bytes < byteColumn) {
                units += byteColumn - bytes;
            }
        }
        return units + (columnsStartAt1 ? 1 : 0);
    }

    #! Returns a line of a file, if the file can be read here
    /** @param file the path of the file
        @param line the 1-based line

        @return the text of the line without its end of line characters, or @ref nothing if the file cannot be
        read here, as for a file of a remote program, or has no such line
    */
    private:internal *string getFileLine(*string file, int line) {
        if (!file || line < 1) {
            return;
        }
        *hash<auto> stat = hstat(file);
        if (!stat || stat.type != "REGULAR") {
            return;
        }
        # the lines of a file are read again when it has changed
        *hash<auto> cached = m_fileLines{file};
        if (!cached || cached.mtime != stat.mtime || cached.size != stat.size) {
            list<string> lines = ();
            try {
                FileLineIterator i(file);
                while (i.next()) {
                    lines += i.getValue();
                }
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                return;
            }
            cached = m_fileLines{file} = {"mtime": stat.mtime, "size": stat.size, "lines": lines};
        }
        return cached.lines[line - 1];
    }

    #! Returns if the columns of the protocol start at 1
    private:internal bool columnsStartAt1() {
        return m_initializeArgs.columnsStartAt1 ?? True;
    }

    #! Returns the name of a thread that is shown in the IDE
    /** @param tid the ID of the thread
        @param name the name of the thread, if known; the default names that %Qore gives threads, \c "qore/"
        <i>tid</i>, and \c "qore" for the initial thread of the process, are not shown
        @param start if the thread started the program

        @return the name of the thread with its ID
    */
    static string getThreadDisplayName(int tid, *string name, bool start) {
        if (name && name !~ /^qore(\/[0-9]+)?$/) {
            return sprintf("%s (%d)", name, tid);
        }
        return start ? sprintf("Main Thread (%d)", tid) : sprintf("Thread %d", tid);
    }

    # get threads provided to vsc
    private:internal list getThreads() {
        return select m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.info.threads, !exists m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.detachedThreads{$1};
    }

    private hash<auto> getCommands() {
        hash cmds = DebugCommandLine::getCommands();
        # any extra commands ?
        return cmds;
    }

    # methods implementing commands "public" is needed bacause of hasCallableMethod()
    public hash vsc_initialize(hash args) {
        m_initializeArgs = args;
        m_programState = hash();
        updateProgramCache(doCommand(("cmd": "program//list")));
        return getCapabilities();
    }

    public nothing vsc_launch(hash args) {
        if (!exists args.program) {
            args.program = defaultProgram;
        }
        hash p = doCommand((
            "cmd": "program//create",
            "filename": args.program,
            "args": args.args ?? (),
        ));
        updateProgramCache(p);
        string pgmId = p.result.firstKey();
        m_currentPgmId = int(pgmId);
        m_programState{pgmId} += (
            "startMethod": START_LAUNCH,
            "launchArgs": args,
            # all threads stop together unless the client disables it; see stopOtherThreads()
            "stopAllThreads": args.stopAllThreads !== False,
            "startThreadId": p.result{pgmId}.threads[0],
        );
        # we are ready receive breakpoints
        sendVscEvent("initialized");
    }

    public nothing vsc_attach(hash args) {
        string pgmId;
        if (!exists args.program) {
            args.program = defaultProgram;
        }
        if (args.program =~ /^[0-9]+$/) {
            pgmId = args.program;
        } else {
            foreach string pgmId2 in (keys m_programState) {
                if (m_programState{pgmId2}.info.scriptName == args.program) {
                    pgmId = pgmId2;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (!exists pgmId) {
                throw "VDA-ERROR", sprintf("Cannot resolve program %y", args.program);
            }
        }
        doCommand((
            "cmd": "program/"+pgmId+"/add",
        ));
        m_currentPgmId = int(pgmId);
        m_programState{pgmId} += (
            "startMethod": START_ATTACH,
            # all threads stop together unless the client disables it; see stopOtherThreads()
            "stopAllThreads": args.stopAllThreads !== False,
        );
        # the program is debugged: the client can set its breakpoints now, before a thread of the program reaches
        # them; a thread that starts before the configuration phase has ended is held until then
        sendVscEvent("initialized");
        sendVscEvent("process", {
            "name": m_programState{pgmId}.info.scriptName,
            "isLocalProcess": False,
            "startMethod": "attach",
        });
        m_programState{pgmId}.vcsNotified = True;
        if (m_programState{pgmId}.info.debugged) {
            # threads that are stopped, such as the thread of a program that a debug server holds until a client
            # attaches; their events are handled when the configuration phase has ended (see vsc_configurationDone())
            # we cannot get what is main thread when attaching
            foreach int tid in (m_programState{pgmId}.info.interrupted) {
                sendVscEvent("thread", ("threadId": tid, "reason": "started"));
                m_programState{pgmId}.vcsThreadNotified{tid} = True;
                m_programState{pgmId}.heldEvents += (tid,);
            }
        }
    }

    public nothing vsc_configurationDone(*hash args) {
        # the configuration phase has ended: the launched program held at its first bootstrap stop (see the
        # attach handling in processEvents()) may now run.  Resume it if it is held; if it has not yet reached
        # that stop, the recorded flag makes it continue at once when it does.  The request and event handling
        # are serialized by m_lock, so the flag and the held event are set and read without a race.
        if (m_currentPgmId && exists m_programState{m_currentPgmId}) {
            m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.bootstrap.configurationDone = True;
            if (exists m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.bootstrap.entryHold) {
                hash<auto> held = remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.bootstrap.entryHold;
                # resume the bootstrap from the attach stop, as the bootstrap stepping (case 1) would have; it
                # steps to the program's first statement, where "stopOnEntry" and any created breakpoint are
                # honoured
                vsc_stepIn(("threadId": held.tid));
            }
            # the threads of an attached program that started during the configuration phase
            foreach int tid in (remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.heldThreads) {
                resumeThread(tid);
            }
            # the threads of an attached program that were stopped when it was attached: their stops are handled as
            # if they had just happened, so a thread that is held when it starts runs, and another one is reported as
            # stopped
            foreach int tid in (remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.heldEvents) {
                processDebugEvent(doCommand(("cmd": "thread/debug/event/get", "tid": tid)).result);
            }
        }
    }

    public hash vsc_threads(*hash args) {
        #debug("pgmid: %y, state: %y", m_currentPgmId, m_programState);
        hash res.threads = ();
        if (m_currentPgmId) {
            updateProgramCache(doCommand(("cmd": "program/="+m_currentPgmId+"/list")));

            foreach int threadId in (getThreads()) {
                push res.threads, {
                    "id": threadId,
                    # the current name of the thread, or the name in its last event when the debug server does not give
                    # the names of threads
                    "name": VscDebugAdapter::getThreadDisplayName(threadId,
                        m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.info.threadNames{threadId}
                            ?? m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.threadNames{threadId},
                        threadId == m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.startThreadId),
                };
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    public vsc_pause(hash args) {
        m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.pauseRequests{args.threadId} = True;
        on_error remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.pauseRequests{args.threadId};
        doCommand(("cmd": "program/"+m_currentPgmId+"/thread/"+args.threadId+"/stop"));
    }

    public hash vsc_continue(hash args) {
        if (!m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.stopAllThreads) {
            resumeThread(args.threadId);
            return {"allThreadsContinued": False};
        }
        # all stopped threads continue; a thread that stops later for a stop that was requested when another
        # thread stopped is resumed (see processDebugEvent())
        remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.allStopRequests;
        resumeThread(args.threadId);
        foreach softint tid in (keys m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread) {
            if (tid == args.threadId) {
                continue;
            }
            try {
                resumeThread(tid);
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                # a thread that a step resumed in the meantime is not stopped
                debug("thread %d not resumed: %s", tid, VscDebugAdapter::getErrorText(ex));
            }
        }
        return {"allThreadsContinued": True};
    }

    #! Resumes a stopped thread
    private:internal resumeThread(softint tid) {
        doCommand(("cmd": "thread/go/run", "tid": tid));
    }

    #! Requests the other running threads of the program to stop, when a thread stops and all threads stop together
    /** Each thread stops at its next statement and is then reported as stopped; a thread that waits, as for input,
        is reported when it runs again.
    */
    private:internal stopOtherThreads(softstring pgmId, int tid) {
        # the threads that the client knows; the program's threads that are cached are those when it was listed
        foreach softint other in (keys m_programState{pgmId}.vcsThreadNotified) {
            if (other == tid || exists m_programState{pgmId}.thread{other}
                || m_programState{pgmId}.pauseRequests{other} || m_programState{pgmId}.allStopRequests{other}) {
                continue;
            }
            *string res = doCommand(("cmd": "program/" + pgmId + "/thread/" + other + "/stop")).result;
            # a thread that has ended in the meantime does not stop
            if (res == "ok") {
                m_programState{pgmId}.allStopRequests{other} = True;
            }
        }
    }

    public vsc_next(hash args) {
        step(args.threadId, "stepover");
    }

    public vsc_stepIn(hash args) {
        if (exists args.targetId) {
            # a target is the entry of the called code: the thread steps over the statement and stops when the
            # statement calls the code
            step(args.threadId, "stepover", {"id": args.targetId});
        } else {
            step(args.threadId, "step");
        }
    }

    #! Returns the calls of the statement of a stack frame that can be stepped into
    /** The ID of a target is the statement ID of the start of the called code; the calls are given for the top frame
        only, as stepping continues the thread from its current statement
    */
    public hash vsc_stepInTargets(hash args) {
        int tid = args.frameId >> 16;
        int frame = args.frameId & 0xffff;
        hash res.targets = ();
        *list l = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{tid}.stack;
        if (!l) {
            l = doCommand((
                "cmd": "thread/stack",
                "tid": tid,
            )).result;
            m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{tid}.stack = l;
        }
        if (frame || !l || !l[0].statementid) {
            return res;
        }
        string path = l[0].file;
        *hash ls = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.loadedSourceByName{getLoadedSourceName(l[0].file, l[0].source)};
        if (ls) {
            path = getSource(ls).path ?? path;
        }
        list<auto> targets = doCommand((
            "cmd": "program/" + m_currentPgmId + "/statement/stepintargets",
            "value": {"id": l[0].statementid},
        )).result ?? ();
        foreach hash<auto> t in (targets) {
            hash<auto> target = {
                "id": t.statement_id,
                "label": t.name,
                "line": t.start_line,
                "endLine": t.end_line,
            };
            if (t.start_column >= 0) {
                target.column = getProtocolColumn(getFileLine(path, t.start_line), t.start_column, columnsStartAt1());
                target.endColumn = getProtocolColumn(getFileLine(path, t.end_line), t.end_column, columnsStartAt1());
            }
            push res.targets, target;
        }
        return res;
    }

    public vsc_stepOut(hash args) {
        step(args.threadId, "untilreturn");
    }

    #! Resumes a thread with a step; the next stop of the thread ends the step (see processDebugEvent())
    /** @param tid the thread
        @param run_state the run state of the step
        @param runTo the statement to run to, if any, as given to the debugger, such as \c id
    */
    private:internal step(int tid, string run_state, *hash<auto> runTo) {
        m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.steppingThreads{tid} = True;
        on_error remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.steppingThreads{tid};
        hash<auto> cmd = {"cmd": "thread/go/" + run_state, "tid": tid};
        if (runTo) {
            cmd.value = runTo;
        }
        doCommand(cmd);
    }

    public hash vsc_stackTrace(hash args) {
        *list l = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{args.threadId}.stack;
        if (!l) {
            l = doCommand((
                "cmd": "thread/stack",
                "tid": args.threadId,
            )).result;
            m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{args.threadId}.stack = l;
        }
        hash res.stackFrames = ();
        res.totalFrames = l.size();
        *int startThreadId = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.startThreadId;
        if (args.threadId == startThreadId) {
            res.totalFrames -= (m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.bootstrap.frameCnt ?? 0);
        } else if (l && l.last().type == "new-thread") {
            # the last frame of another thread is the call of the code of the thread by the operator that started
            # the thread, such as the background operator; its location is where the thread was started, in another
            # thread, and it is the location of the frame above it
            --res.totalFrames;
        }
        int n = args.levels ?? 0;
        if (n == 0) {
            n = res.totalFrames;
        }
        for (int i = args.startFrame ?? 0; n > 0 && i < res.totalFrames; i++, n--) {
            # args.format not supported now
            hash sf;
            sf.id = (args.threadId << 16) + i; # an identifier for the stack frame. It must be unique across all threads.
            # each frame of the call stack gives a function and the location of its call, which is in the function of
            # the next frame; the location of the first frame is the statement the thread stopped at
            sf.name = (i + 1 < l.size() && (i + 1 < res.totalFrames || args.threadId != startThreadId))
                ? l[i + 1].function
                : TopLevelFrameName;
            *hash ls = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.loadedSourceByName{getLoadedSourceName(l[i].file, l[i].source)};
            if (exists ls) {
                sf.source = getSource(ls);
            } else {
                sf.source.path = l[i].file;
                sf.source.sourceReference = 0;
                sf.source.presentationHint = "deemphasize";
            }
            sf.line = l[i].line;
            sf.endLine = l[i].endline;
            if (exists l[i].column) {
                # the frame's statement, where it is known
                string path = sf.source.path ?? l[i].file;
                sf.column = getProtocolColumn(getFileLine(path, l[i].line), l[i].column, columnsStartAt1());
                sf.endColumn = getProtocolColumn(getFileLine(path, l[i].endline), l[i].endcolumn, columnsStartAt1());
            } else {
                sf.column = 0;
            }
            #sf.moduleId
            push res.stackFrames, sf;
        }
        return res;
    }

    public hash vsc_exceptionInfo(hash args) {
        hash res;
        *hash ex = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{args.threadId}.exception;
        if (ex) {
            res.exceptionId = ex.err;
            res.description = ex.desc;
            res.breakMode = "always";    # 'never' | 'always' | 'unhandled' | 'userUnhandled';
            res.details.message = ex.desc;
            res.details.typeName = ex.err;
            res.details.stackTrace = sprintf("%Y", ex);
        } else {
            res.exceptionId = "N/A";
            res.breakMode = "never";
        }
        return res;
    }

    public hash vsc_scopes(hash args) {
        int threadId = args.frameId >> 16;
        int frameId = args.frameId & 0xFFFF;
        hash res.scopes = ();
        push res.scopes, {
            "name": "Locals",
            "variablesReference": args.frameId,
            "expensive": False,
            "namedVariables": getFrameLocals(threadId, frameId).size(),
        };
        push res.scopes, {
            "name": "Globals",
            # the global variables are read with the stopped thread
            "variablesReference": getVarRef(threadId, frameId, {"scope": "globals"}, ()),
            "expensive": False,
            "namedVariables": getGlobals().size(),
        };
        return res;
    }

    #! Returns the names of the local variables of a frame of a stopped thread, which are loaded when needed
    private:internal list getFrameLocals(int threadId, int frameId) {
        *list l = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.locals{frameId};
        if (exists l) {
            return l;
        }
        try {
            l = doCommand((
                "cmd": "thread/local//list",
                "tid": threadId,
                "frameid": frameId,
            )).result;
            if (frameId == 0 && exists m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.debugVar) {
                push l, DEBUGVAR_PREFIX+m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.debugVar;
            }
            m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.locals{frameId} = l;
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            debug("cannot list the local variables of thread %d frame %d: %s", threadId, frameId,
                get_exception_string(ex));
        }
        return l ?? ();
    }

    #! Returns the names of the global variables of the program, which are loaded when needed
    private:internal list getGlobals() {
        *list l = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{0}.globals;
        if (exists l) {
            return l;
        }
        try {
            l = doCommand((
                "cmd": "program/"+m_currentPgmId+"/global//list",
            )).result;
            m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{0}.globals = l;
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            debug("cannot list the global variables: %s", get_exception_string(ex));
        }
        return l ?? ();
    }

    #! Returns the variables of a scope or the elements, keys or members of a structured value
    /** Lists, hashes and objects are shown as trees: each has a variable reference whose children are read from the
        stopped thread when they are shown; the elements of lists are paged with \c start and \c count
    */
    public hash vsc_variables(hash args) {
        hash res.variables = ();
        int ref = args.variablesReference;
        if (ref < VarRefBase) {
            # the local variables of a frame
            if (args.filter == "indexed") {
                return res;
            }
            int threadId = ref >> 16;
            int frameId = ref & 0xFFFF;
            foreach string name in (VscDebugAdapter::page(getFrameLocals(threadId, frameId), args)) {
                hash<auto> root = VscDebugAdapter::getRootForName(name);
                push res.variables, makeVariable(threadId, frameId, root, (), name,
                    describeVariable(threadId, frameId, root, ()), root.local);
            }
            return res;
        }
        hash<auto> vr = getVarRefInfo(ref);
        if (vr.root.scope == "globals") {
            if (args.filter == "indexed") {
                return res;
            }
            foreach string name in (VscDebugAdapter::page(getGlobals(), args)) {
                hash<auto> root = {"global": name};
                push res.variables, makeVariable(vr.tid, vr.frameId, root, (), name,
                    describeVariable(vr.tid, vr.frameId, root, ()), name);
            }
            return res;
        }
        hash<auto> d = doCommand((
            "cmd": "thread/variable/get",
            "tid": vr.tid,
            "frameid": vr.frameId,
            "root": vr.root,
            "path": vr.path,
            "children": True,
            "start": args.start ?? 0,
            "count": args.count ?: NOTHING,
        )).result;
        # a list has only indexed children, hashes and objects only named ones
        if ((args.filter == "named" && d.indexed) || (args.filter == "indexed" && !d.indexed)) {
            return res;
        }
        foreach hash<auto> child in (d.children) {
            push res.variables, makeVariable(vr.tid, vr.frameId, vr.root, vr.path + (child.key,), child.name, child,
                VscDebugAdapter::getChildEvaluateName(vr.evaluateName, d, child.key));
        }
        return res;
    }

    #! Sets the value of a variable or of an element, key or member of a structured value
    public hash vsc_setVariable(hash args) {
        int ref = args.variablesReference;
        int threadId;
        int frameId;
        hash<auto> root;
        list<auto> path = ();
        *string evaluate_name;
        if (ref < VarRefBase) {
            threadId = ref >> 16;
            frameId = ref & 0xFFFF;
            root = VscDebugAdapter::getRootForName(args.name);
            evaluate_name = root.local;
        } else {
            hash<auto> vr = getVarRefInfo(ref);
            threadId = vr.tid;
            frameId = vr.frameId;
            if (vr.root.scope == "globals") {
                root = {"global": args.name};
                evaluate_name = args.name;
            } else {
                root = vr.root;
                path = vr.path + (args.name,);
            }
        }
        hash<auto> d = doCommand((
            "cmd": "thread/variable/set",
            "tid": threadId,
            "frameid": frameId,
            "root": root,
            "path": path,
            # the value is a Qore expression, evaluated with the variables of the frame
            "expression": args.value,
        )).result;
        hash<auto> v = makeVariable(threadId, frameId, root, path, args.name, d, evaluate_name);
        remove v.name;
        remove v.evaluateName;
        return v;
    }

    #! Evaluates an expression with the variables of a frame of a stopped thread
    /** In the debug console, a line whose first word is a debugger command is processed as the command; a line that
        starts with \c "$" is evaluated without the \c "$"
    */
    public hash vsc_evaluate(hash args) {
        string expr = args.expression;
        if (args.context == "repl") {
            if (expr =~ /^\$/) {
                splice expr, 0, 1;
            } else if (isDebuggerCommand(expr)) {
                processCmdLine(expr);
                return {"result": "", "variablesReference": 0};
            }
        }
        if (!exists args.frameId) {
            throw "VSC-EVALUATE-ERROR", "an expression is evaluated with a frame of a stopped thread; select a frame";
        }
        int threadId = args.frameId >> 16;
        int frameId = args.frameId & 0xFFFF;
        hash<auto> d = evaluateInThread(threadId, expr, frameId);
        hash<auto> v = makeVariable(threadId, frameId, {"eval": d.id}, (), expr, d);
        return {"result": v.value, "type": v.type, "variablesReference": v.variablesReference}
            + v{"indexedVariables", "namedVariables"};
    }

    #! Returns True if the first word of the given line is a debugger command
    private:internal bool isDebuggerCommand(string line) {
        *string word = (line =~ x/^\s*(\S+)/)[0];
        hash<auto> commands = getCommands();
        return exists word && exists commands{">"}{word};
    }

    #! Returns a description of a variable or of an element, key or member of a structured value
    private:internal hash<auto> describeVariable(int threadId, int frameId, hash<auto> root, list<auto> path) {
        return doCommand((
            "cmd": "thread/variable/get",
            "tid": threadId,
            "frameid": frameId,
            "root": root,
            "path": path,
        )).result;
    }

    #! Returns a variable of the protocol for a description of a value
    /** A list, hash or object gets a variable reference whose children are read when they are shown
    */
    private:internal hash<auto> makeVariable(int threadId, int frameId, hash<auto> root, list<auto> path,
            string name, hash<auto> d, *string evaluate_name) {
        hash<auto> v = {"name": name, "value": d.value, "type": d.type, "variablesReference": 0};
        if (d.indexed || d.named) {
            v.variablesReference = getVarRef(threadId, frameId, root, path, evaluate_name);
            if (d.indexed) {
                v.indexedVariables = d.indexed;
            }
            if (d.named) {
                v.namedVariables = d.named;
            }
        }
        if (evaluate_name) {
            v.evaluateName = evaluate_name;
        }
        return v;
    }

    #! Returns a new variable reference for a structured value of a stopped thread
    /** The references of a thread are valid while it is stopped; see removeVarRefs()
    */
    private:internal int getVarRef(int threadId, int frameId, hash<auto> root, list<auto> path,
            *string evaluate_name) {
        int ref = m_nextVarRef++;
        m_varRefs{ref} = {
            "tid": threadId,
            "frameId": frameId,
            "root": root,
            "path": path,
            "evaluateName": evaluate_name,
        };
        return ref;
    }

    #! Returns the structured value of a variable reference
    /** @throw VSC-VARIABLE-ERROR the reference is not valid, as its thread has resumed
    */
    private:internal hash<auto> getVarRefInfo(int ref) {
        *hash<auto> vr = m_varRefs{ref};
        if (!vr) {
            throw "VSC-VARIABLE-ERROR", sprintf("invalid variable reference %d; the thread has resumed", ref);
        }
        return vr;
    }

    #! Removes the variable references of a thread that resumes
    private:internal removeVarRefs(int threadId) {
        m_varRefs -= (map $1.key, m_varRefs.pairIterator(), $1.value.tid == threadId);
    }

    #! Returns the root of a variable path for the name of a variable of a frame
    static hash<auto> getRootForName(string name) {
        return name =~ /^\$/ ? {"debug": name.substr(1)} : {"local": name};
    }

    #! Returns the expression of an element, key or member of a structured value, if the value has one
    static *string getChildEvaluateName(*string parent, hash<auto> d, auto key) {
        if (!parent) {
            return;
        }
        if (d.indexed) {
            return sprintf("%s[%d]", parent, key);
        }
        if (d.type =~ /^hash/) {
            return sprintf("%s{%y}", parent, key);
        }
        return key =~ /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$/ ? sprintf("%s.%s", parent, key) : NOTHING;
    }

    #! Returns the part of a list given by the \c start and \c count arguments of a request
    static list<auto> page(list<auto> l, hash args) {
        int start = args.start ?? 0;
        return args.count ? l[start..(start + args.count - 1)] : l[start..];
    }

    public hash vsc_completions(hash args) {
        # auto complete for debug console
        hash res.targets = ();
        if (args.text[0] == "$") {
            # variable
            int threadId = (args.frameId ?? 0) >> 16;
            int frameId = (args.frameId ?? 0) & 0xFFFF;
            *list l;
            if (threadId == 0) {
                l = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{0}.globals ?? ();
            } else {
                l = (m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{threadId}.locals{frameId} ?? ()) + (m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.thread{0}.globals ?? ());
            }
            string ss = args.text.substr(1, args.column-2);
            # args.column, line
            foreach string s in (l) {
                if (bindex(s, ss) >= 0) {
                    hash c;
                    c.label = s;
                    # c.text
                    c.type = "variable";
                    push res.targets, c;
                }
            }
        } else {
            # command line command
            foreach string s in (getLineCompletions(args.text.substr(0, args.column-1))) {
                list ll = s.split(" ");
                hash c;
                c.label = pop ll;
                # c.text
                c.type = "text";
                push res.targets, c;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    #! Returns the ID and the file of a source of the protocol, as the program knows the file
    private:internal hash<auto> getSourceFile(hash<auto> source) {
        string sourceId = source.path;
        string file = sourceId;
        if (source.sourceReference > 0) { # always ?? Probably not when launching script
            *hash ls = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.loadedSourceById{source.sourceReference};
            if (ls) {
                sourceId = string(ls.id);
                file = ls.file;
            }
        }
        return {"sourceId": sourceId, "file": file};
    }

    #! Returns the line and the column of the protocol of a statement
    /** @param file the file of the statement, whose lines are read for the conversion of the column
        @param info the @ref Qore::StatementInfo "StatementInfo" of the statement
    */
    private:internal hash<auto> getStatementPosition(string file, hash<auto> info) {
        hash<auto> rv = {"line": info.start_line};
        if (info.start_column >= 0) {
            rv.column = getProtocolColumn(getFileLine(file, info.start_line), info.start_column, columnsStartAt1());
        }
        return rv;
    }

    public hash vsc_setBreakpoints(hash args) {
        hash<auto> sf = getSourceFile(args.source);
        string sourceId = sf.sourceId;
        string file = sf.file;
        deleteBreakpoints(m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.sourceBreakpoints{sourceId});
        remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.sourceBreakpoints{sourceId};
        hash res.breakpoints = ();
        if (args.breakpoints) {
            list bkpts;
            foreach hash b in (args.breakpoints) {
                # the debugger checks the condition, hit condition and log message of the breakpoint
                hash<auto> bkpt = {"file": file, "lineno": b.line} + b{"condition", "hitCondition", "logMessage"};
                # a breakpoint on a statement of a line with more than one statement
                if (exists b.column) {
                    bkpt.column = getByteColumn(getFileLine(file, b.line), b.column, columnsStartAt1());
                }
                push bkpts, bkpt;
            }
            res.breakpoints = setBreakpoints(bkpts);
            foreach hash b in (\res.breakpoints) {
                if (b.verified) {
                    # the IDE shows a column breakpoint at the statement that it is set on
                    if (exists args.breakpoints[$#].column && b.statementId) {
                        hash<auto> info = doCommand((
                            "cmd": "program/" + m_currentPgmId + "/statement/get",
                            "value": {"id": b.statementId},
                        )).result;
                        b += getStatementPosition(file, info);
                    }
                    m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.sourceBreakpoints{sourceId}{b.id} = b + args.breakpoints[$#];
                    remove b.statementId;
                }
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    #! Returns the locations of a range of lines where breakpoints can be set
    /** Each statement that starts on a line of the range is a location, so a line with more than one statement has
        more than one location
    */
    public hash vsc_breakpointLocations(hash args) {
        string file = getSourceFile(args.source).file;
        int endLine = args.endLine ?? args.line;
        hash res.breakpoints = ();
        for (int line = args.line; line <= endLine; ++line) {
            list<auto> stmts;
            try {
                stmts = doCommand((
                    "cmd": "program/" + m_currentPgmId + "/statement/list",
                    "value": {"file": file, "lineno": line},
                )).result ?? ();
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                # the file is not a source of the program
                break;
            }
            foreach hash<auto> stmt in (stmts) {
                # only statements that start on the line, not one that contains it
                if (stmt.start_line != line && stmt.start_line + stmt.offset != line) {
                    continue;
                }
                hash<auto> pos = getStatementPosition(file, stmt);
                pos.line = line;
                # the columns of the range are on its first and last lines
                if (pos.column) {
                    if ((line == args.line && exists args.column && pos.column < args.column)
                        || (line == endLine && exists args.endColumn && pos.column > args.endColumn)) {
                        continue;
                    }
                }
                push res.breakpoints, pos;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    public hash vsc_setFunctionBreakpoints(hash args) {
        deleteBreakpoints(m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.functionBreakpoints);
        remove m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.functionBreakpoints;
        hash res.breakpoints = ();
        if (args.breakpoints) {
            list bkpts;
            foreach hash b in (args.breakpoints) {
                *list l = b.name =~ x/^(.+)\((.*)\)$/;
                if (l) {
                    list la = ();
                    foreach string s2 in (split(',', l[1])) {
                        s2 = trim(s2);
                        if (s2 != "") {
                            push la, s2;
                        }
                    }
                    push bkpts, ("function": l[0], "args": la) + b{"condition", "hitCondition"};
                } else {
                    # a function given by its name only: the breakpoint is on the function's only variant
                    push bkpts, ("function": b.name) + b{"condition", "hitCondition"};
                }
            }
            res.breakpoints = setBreakpoints(bkpts);
            foreach hash b in (\res.breakpoints) {
                if (b.verified) {
                    m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.functionBreakpoints{b.id} = b + args.breakpoints[$#];
                    remove b.statementId;
                }
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    public vsc_setExceptionBreakpoints(hash args) {
        m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.exceptionBreakpoints.filters = args.filters;
        # args.exceptionOptions
    }

    public hash vsc_modules(hash args) {
        int n = args.totalModules;
        if (!n) {
            n = m_programState.size();
        }
        hash res.modules = ();
        for (int i = args.startModule ?? 0; i < m_programState.size() && n > 0; i++, n--) {
            push res.modules, getModule((keys m_programState)[i]);
        }
        res.totalModules = m_programState.size();
        return res;
    }

    public hash vsc_loadedSources(*hash args) {
        hash res.sources = ();
        if (m_currentPgmId) {
            foreach string id in (keys m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.loadedSourceById) {
                push res.sources, getSource(m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.loadedSourceById{id});
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    public hash vsc_source(hash args) {
        hash res;
        if (m_currentPgmId) { # or do we need it global ?
            *hash ls = m_programState{m_currentPgmId}.loadedSourceById{args.sourceReference};
            if (exists ls.source) {
                res.content = doCommand((
                    "cmd": "program/"+m_currentPgmId+"/label/source",
                    "label": ls.file,
                )).result.code;
            } else if (exists ls.file) {
                res.content = doCommand((
                    "cmd": "program/"+m_currentPgmId+"/file/source",
                    "file": ls.file,
                )).result.code;
            }
        }
        if (!exists res.content) {
            res.content = '';
        }
        return res;
    }

    public vsc_disconnect(*hash args) {
        m_running = False;
        # terminate debugger
        # args.terminateDebuggee not supported
        doCommand(("cmd": "shutdown"));
        sendVscEvent("terminated");
    }

    private:internal hash getCapabilities() {
        hash cap = (
            /* The debug adapter supports the configurationDoneRequest. */
            "supportsConfigurationDoneRequest": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports function breakpoints. */
            "supportsFunctionBreakpoints": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports conditional breakpoints. */
            "supportsConditionalBreakpoints": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports breakpoints that break execution
                after a specified number of hits. */
            "supportsHitConditionalBreakpoints": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports a (side effect free) evaluate
                request for data hovers. */
            "supportsEvaluateForHovers": True,

            /* Available filters or options for the setExceptionBreakpoints request. */
            "exceptionBreakpointFilters": (
                (
                    "filter": "User",
                    "label": "User exception",
                ),
                (
                    "filter": "System",
                    "label": "System exception",
                ),
                (
                    "filter": "uncaught",
                    "label": "Uncaught exceptions",
                    "description": "Exceptions that no try statement of the debugged code catches",
                ),
            ),

            /* The debug adapter supports stepping back via the stepBack and
                reverseContinue requests. */
            "supportsStepBack": False,

            /* The debug adapter supports setting a variable to a value. */
            "supportsSetVariable": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports restarting a frame. */
            "supportsRestartFrame": False,

            /* The debug adapter supports the gotoTargetsRequest. */
            "supportsGotoTargetsRequest": False,

            /* The debug adapter supports the stepInTargetsRequest. */
            "supportsStepInTargetsRequest": True,
            "supportsBreakpointLocationsRequest": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports the completionsRequest. */
            "supportsCompletionsRequest": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports the modules request. */
            "supportsModulesRequest": True,  # not supported in IDE ?

            /* The set of additional module information exposed by the debug adapter. */
            #"additionalModuleColumns": ColumnDescriptor[],

            /* Checksum algorithms supported by the debug adapter. */
            "supportedChecksumAlgorithms": ('SHA1'),

            /* The debug adapter supports the RestartRequest. In this case
                a client should not implement 'restart' by terminating and
                relaunching the adapter but by calling the RestartRequest. */
            "supportsRestartRequest": False,

            /* The debug adapter supports 'exceptionOptions' on the
                setExceptionBreakpoints request. */
            "supportsExceptionOptions": False,

            /* The debug adapter supports a 'format' attribute on the
                stackTraceRequest, variablesRequest, and evaluateRequest. */
            "supportsValueFormattingOptions": False,  # not supported in IDE ?

            /* The debug adapter supports the exceptionInfo request. */
            "supportsExceptionInfoRequest": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports the 'terminateDebuggee' attribute
                on the 'disconnect' request. */
            "supportTerminateDebuggee": False,

            /* The debug adapter supports the delayed loading of parts of the stack,
                which requires that both the 'startFrame' and 'levels' arguments and
                the 'totalFrames' result of the 'StackTrace' request are supported. */
            "supportsDelayedStackTraceLoading": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports the 'loadedSources' request. */
            "supportsLoadedSourcesRequest": True,

            /* The debug adapter supports logpoints by interpreting the 'logMessage' attribute of the SourceBreakpoint. */
            "supportsLogPoints": True,

        );
        return cap;
    }

}
}
